<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Though hot the fight, why quit the field?</l><l>Why must I either fly or yield,</l><l>Since Jesus is my mighty shield?</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>When creature comforts fade and die,</l><l>Worldlings may weep, but why should I?</l><l>Jesus still lives, and still is nigh.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Though all the flocks and herds were dead,</l><l>My soul a famine need not dread,</l><l>For Jesus is my living bread.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>I know not what may soon betide,</l><l>Or how my wants shall be supplied;</l><l>But Jesus knows, and will provide.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>Though sin would fill me with distress,</l><l>The throne of grace I dare address,</l><l>For Jesus is my righteousness.</l></lg>
<lg label="7."><l>Though faint my prayers and cold my love,</l><l>My steadfast hope shall not remove,</l><l>While Jesus intercedes above.</l></lg>
<lg label="8."><l>Against me earth and hell combine;</l><l>But on my side is power divine;</l><l>Jesus is all, and He is mine!</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
